      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority will formally overrule Williams v. Florida because the Sixth Amendment's original public meaning makes twelve members an essential feature of the jury for serious criminal offenses, and will hold that this protection applies equally to state prosecutions through the Fourteenth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority will announce a categorical twelve-member requirement for juries initially empaneled to try serious criminal offenses, not a rule limited to Florida, Kian's particular offenses, or proof that a smaller jury actually impaired deliberations; it will leave civil-jury size and later emergency juror excusals unresolved."
    }
  ],
